result:
Postgres. Three-phase expand/backfill/contract. Every step guarded → safe re-run.

Assumptions:
- `users(id bigint PK, full_name text)`
- Split rule: first token → `first_name`, rest → `last_name`. Single-word name → `last_name` NULL.
- `full_name` stays until app reads new columns. Drop in separate migration.

## 001_expand_and_backfill.sql

```sql
-- Run OUTSIDE a transaction block (psql -f, or tool's "no transaction" mode),
-- because the backfill loop COMMITs per batch. Requires PG 11+.

-- 1. Expand: add columns (no-op if present)
ALTER TABLE users ADD COLUMN IF NOT EXISTS first_name text;
ALTER TABLE users ADD COLUMN IF NOT EXISTS last_name  text;

-- 2. Split function: single source of truth for backfill + trigger
CREATE OR REPLACE FUNCTION split_full_name(
    p_full   text,
    OUT first text,
    OUT last  text
) LANGUAGE sql IMMUTABLE AS $$
    WITH n AS (
        SELECT btrim(regexp_replace(coalesce(p_full, ''), '\s+', ' ', 'g')) AS v
    )
    SELECT coalesce(substring(v FROM '^(\S+)'), ''),   -- never NULL
           substring(v FROM '^\S+\s+(.*)$')            -- NULL if one word
    FROM n;
$$;

-- 3. Dual-write trigger: keep new columns in sync while old code still writes full_name
CREATE OR REPLACE FUNCTION users_sync_name_parts() RETURNS trigger
LANGUAGE plpgsql AS $$
BEGIN
    IF NEW.full_name IS NOT NULL
       AND (TG_OP = 'INSERT'
            OR NEW.full_name IS DISTINCT FROM OLD.full_name)
       AND NEW.first_name IS NOT DISTINCT FROM
           CASE WHEN TG_OP = 'INSERT' THEN NULL ELSE OLD.first_name END
    THEN
        SELECT s.first, s.last
          INTO NEW.first_name, NEW.last_name
          FROM split_full_name(NEW.full_name) s;
    END IF;
    RETURN NEW;
END;
$$;

DROP TRIGGER IF EXISTS trg_users_sync_name_parts ON users;
CREATE TRIGGER trg_users_sync_name_parts
    BEFORE INSERT OR UPDATE OF full_name ON users
    FOR EACH ROW EXECUTE FUNCTION users_sync_name_parts();

-- 4. Backfill in batches. Only touches unprocessed rows.
--    Termination guaranteed: split always yields non-NULL first_name,
--    so every updated row leaves the WHERE set.
DO $$
DECLARE
    batch_size constant int := 5000;
    rows_done  int;
BEGIN
    LOOP
        WITH todo AS (
            SELECT id
              FROM users
             WHERE first_name IS NULL
               AND full_name  IS NOT NULL
             ORDER BY id
             LIMIT batch_size
             FOR UPDATE SKIP LOCKED
        )
        UPDATE users u
           SET first_name = s.first,
               last_name  = s.last
          FROM todo, LATERAL split_full_name(u.full_name) s
         WHERE u.id = todo.id;

        GET DIAGNOSTICS rows_done = ROW_COUNT;
        COMMIT;                       -- release locks, limit WAL/bloat per batch
        EXIT WHEN rows_done = 0;
        PERFORM pg_sleep(0.05);       -- throttle replication lag
    END LOOP;
END;
$$;

-- 5. Verify (should return 0)
SELECT count(*) AS unbackfilled
  FROM users
 WHERE first_name IS NULL AND full_name IS NOT NULL;
```

## 002_contract.sql (later, after app reads/writes first/last only)

```sql
BEGIN;

-- Refuse to drop if backfill incomplete
DO $$
BEGIN
    IF EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM information_schema.columns
                WHERE table_name = 'users' AND column_name = 'full_name')
       AND EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM users
                    WHERE first_name IS NULL AND full_name IS NOT NULL)
    THEN
        RAISE EXCEPTION 'Backfill incomplete; aborting contract step';
    END IF;
END;
$$;

DROP TRIGGER IF EXISTS trg_users_sync_name_parts ON users;
DROP FUNCTION IF EXISTS users_sync_name_parts();
DROP FUNCTION IF EXISTS split_full_name(text);

ALTER TABLE users DROP COLUMN IF EXISTS full_name;

COMMIT;
```

## 001_down.sql (rollback of expand)

```sql
DROP TRIGGER IF EXISTS trg_users_sync_name_parts ON users;
DROP FUNCTION IF EXISTS users_sync_name_parts();
DROP FUNCTION IF EXISTS split_full_name(text);
ALTER TABLE users DROP COLUMN IF EXISTS last_name;
ALTER TABLE users DROP COLUMN IF EXISTS first_name;
```

## Why re-runnable

| Step | Guard |
|---|---|
| Add columns | `IF NOT EXISTS` |
| Functions | `CREATE OR REPLACE` |
| Trigger | `DROP ... IF EXISTS` then create |
| Backfill | `WHERE first_name IS NULL` → done rows skipped; crash mid-run resumes from where it stopped |
| Contract | aborts if unbackfilled rows; `DROP ... IF EXISTS` |

## Notes

- `ADD COLUMN` nullable, no default → metadata-only, no table rewrite.
- Trigger only fills split columns when caller didn't set `first_name` itself → new code writing first/last directly not clobbered.
- Name splitting lossy by nature ("Mary Ann van der Berg", mononyms, family-name-first cultures). Consider letting users correct; don't regenerate `full_name` by concatenation as truth.
- Migration tool wraps in transaction (Flyway, Rails, Alembic default)? `COMMIT` inside `DO` errors. Either disable transaction for this migration, or move step 4 to app-level script looping same `UPDATE` with commit per batch.
- Need `NOT NULL` on `first_name`? Add in contract step via `ADD CONSTRAINT ... CHECK (first_name IS NOT NULL) NOT VALID` → `VALIDATE CONSTRAINT` → `SET NOT NULL` to avoid long lock.
